Third-party files in muse/data/

Both files are unmodified copies, distributed under the MIT licenses reproduced below. Each is
identical to the upstream file at the commit given.

alfworld_3prompts.json
  From ReAct (Yao et al., 2023), https://github.com/ysymyth/ReAct, prompts/alfworld_3prompts.json
  at commit 6bdb3a1fd38b8188fc7ba4102969fe483df8fdc9. Reflexion ships the same file as
  alfworld_runs/prompts/alfworld_3prompts.json.
  Copyright (c) 2023 Shunyu Yao. MIT License (ReAct, below).

reflexion_few_shot_examples.txt
  From Reflexion (Shinn et al., 2023), https://github.com/noahshinn/reflexion,
  alfworld_runs/reflexion_few_shot_examples.txt at commit 218cf0ef1df84b05ce379dd4a8e47f17766733a0.
  Copyright (c) 2023 Noah Shinn. MIT License (Reflexion, below).

Also derived from these repositories (short text and logic in muse/, under the same licenses):

  From ReAct:
    muse/prompts.py  ACTOR_INSTRUCTION (the opening line of the actor prompt)
    muse/env.py      TASK_PREFIXES (task type -> few-shot prompt key), process_obs and
                     process_initial_obs (observation clean-up)
  From Reflexion:
    muse/prompts.py  FAIL_REFLECTION (the failure-reflection query, verbatim) and SUCCESS_REFLECTION_REFLEXION
                     (that query rewritten for success)
    muse/agents.py   the actor's retry schedule (Reflexion: temperature 0.2 x retry; here added to
                     agent.actor_temperature)

